  "limitations": [
    "Baselines (a)-(c) are the frozen 39-case evalsuite run policy-only (sandbox mode, authority violations recorded not enforced). The mapping a=baseline, b=lockdown, c=context_bound is this script's reading of the operator's list; the live authority stack is NOT used and would be circular (registry decides and defines harm).",
    "Same-author synthetic fixtures; scripted proposals; no model in the loop for (a)-(c); in-process latency only (not end to end, not GB10). Latency is wall-clock on a shared dev host and varies run to run.",
    "Small N: heldout has 17 cases, 8 substantive attacks and 3 benign; Wilson 95% intervals are wide and differences between adjacent baselines are mostly inside them.",
    "evalsuite.py was developed after seeing results once (adapter fidelity fix, docs/EVALSUITE.md): context_bound numbers are a development result, not an independent held-out one.",
    "tool-call JSON validity is not applicable to (a)-(c): their proposals are scripted dicts, not model output.",
    "(d)-(f), when run, use the three modelreplay fixture scenarios (invoice_redirect, ticket_exfil, log_secret_post), NOT the 39-case suite, so the dev/heldout split does not apply to them and they are not directly comparable with (a)-(c).",
    "'Triage' in (d)-(f) means the model proposes the single tool call (modelreplay prompt); the context_bound guard then judges it. There is no separate triage-classification experiment.",
    "Model provenance and data labels are heuristic string matching (llm.trace_provenance / infer_labels), not runtime-supplied provenance. Replay mode is model_sampled_policy_replay, not per-branch inference.",
    "At temperature 0 repeated trials are near-identical (effectively one sample per scenario and kind); use --temperature and --seed for variance and record both.",
    "Parse failures and transport failures are non-actions: never counted as blocked attacks or completed work (DECISIONS 11). Attack success is reported over all trials and over parsed proposals only.",
    "The mixed harness routes by a deterministic risk rule (classify_risk). All three fixture scenarios use a sensitive tool, so every trial routes to Lightning; (f) differs from (e) only when a low-risk task exists or Lightning is unreachable (sensitive tasks are then held for a human, never sent to Nano)."
  ]
